<section id="ingredients" aria-labelledby="ing-title" style="padding: clamp(48px, 6vw, 88px) 0">
<div style="max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px); box-sizing: border-box; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 32px 64px">
<div style="flex: 1 1 300px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: #2F5233">KEY INGREDIENTS</p>
<h2 id="ing-title" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 34px); line-height: 1.3; color: #12324F">Key ingredients</h2>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">These are the ingredients shown on the front of the package. This is a general cosmetic, not a functional cosmetic.</p>
</div>
<div style="flex: 999 1 560px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
<p style="margin: 0; border-left: 3px solid #56626D; padding: 4px 0 4px 12px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; color: #56626D">The ‘What research shows’ notes below summarize research on each raw material. They are not tests of NEUVELIF products, and most of the research used leave-on products or other forms. This product is a rinse-off cleanser, so ingredients stay on the skin only briefly.</p>
<div style="background: #2F5233; color: #FFFFFF; padding: clamp(22px, 2.5vw, 32px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: #CFE3C9">KEY INGREDIENT</p>
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 34px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; line-height: 1.1">MATCHA PDRN</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700">Matcha-derived PDRN (sodium DNA)</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: #DCE9D8">DNA fragments (polydeoxyribonucleotide) obtained from matcha. Contains 0.01 ppm.</p>
</div>
<div style="background: #3A6340; padding: 12px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #CFE3C9">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #F0F6EE">Most PDRN research involves salmon-derived PDRN used as injections. Reviews note that research on applying plant-derived PDRN to the skin is still at an early stage.</p>
<a href="https://mdpi-res.com/d_attachment/jfb/jfb-17-00351/article_deploy/jfb-17-00351.pdf" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #CFE3C9; text-underline-offset: 3px">Review of plant-derived PN/PDRN, Journal of Functional Biomaterials, 2026 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(240px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 12px">
<div style="border: 1px solid #D5E0E8; border-top: 3px solid #2F5233; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #56626D">CAFFEINE</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: #12324F">Caffeine</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">An ingredient found in coffee and tea, known to penetrate the skin well.</p>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #D5E0E8; padding-top: 10px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #2F5233">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">It is widely used in cosmetics because of research on microcirculation and antioxidant activity, though many of these studies are reportedly cell or animal studies.</p>
<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23075568/" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #56626D; text-underline-offset: 3px">Herman A·Herman AP, Skin Pharmacology and Physiology, 2013 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
<div style="border: 1px solid #D5E0E8; border-top: 3px solid #2F5233; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #56626D">ESCIN</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: #12324F">Escin</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">A saponin obtained from the seeds of the horse chestnut (marronnier).</p>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #D5E0E8; padding-top: 10px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #2F5233">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">Studies in which people with weak leg venous circulation took horse chestnut seed extract (main component: escin) as capsules are summarized as showing reduced leg swelling. These were not studies of leave-on or rinse-off products.</p>
<a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7144685/" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #56626D; text-underline-offset: 3px">Pittler MH·Ernst E, Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews, 2012 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
<div style="border: 1px solid #D5E0E8; border-top: 3px solid #2F5233; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #56626D">LOW MOLECULAR HYALURONIC ACID</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: #12324F">Low-molecular-weight hyaluronic acid</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">A broken-down form of a classic moisturizing ingredient that holds water in the skin.</p>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #D5E0E8; padding-top: 10px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #2F5233">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">In a study applying 0.1% hyaluronic acid cream for 60 days, skin hydration and elasticity improved, and smaller molecules are described as penetrating the skin better.</p>
<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22052267/" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #56626D; text-underline-offset: 3px">Pavicic T et al., Journal of Drugs in Dermatology, 2011 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
<div style="border: 1px solid #D5E0E8; border-top: 3px solid #2F5233; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #56626D">CERAMIDE NP</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: #12324F">Ceramide NP</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">A lipid that fills the spaces in the skin's stratum corneum.</p>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #D5E0E8; padding-top: 10px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #2F5233">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">Ceramides are epidermal lipids important to skin barrier function and are described as being used in skincare products to replenish them.</p>
<a href="https://www.em-consulte.com/article/903128/the-structure-function-and-importance-of-ceramides" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #56626D; text-underline-offset: 3px">Meckfessel MH·Brandt S, Journal of the American Academy of Dermatology, 2014 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

