<div style="flex: 999 1 560px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; border-top: 2px solid #12324F"><div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">It doesn't foam.</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">That is normal. It is a milk-type cleanser that you spread on without foaming to dissolve makeup and impurities. It contains mild cleansing ingredients such as decyl glucoside.</p>
</div><div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">Do I need to double cleanse?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">Sunscreen and light makeup come off with one wash of the cleansing milk. If you wore heavy makeup or waterproof products, remove them first with a dedicated remover or wash once more after the cleansing milk.</p>
</div><div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">Does it remove waterproof mascara?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">It's hard to remove completely in one go. Remove waterproof eye and lip makeup first with a point makeup remover.</p>
</div><div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">I don't really notice the depuffing effect.</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">The depuffing effect is temporary, and how much you notice it varies from person to person. In a test by the Korea Institute of Dermatological Sciences, facial volume in 22 women decreased by an average of 0.47 cc right after one use (measured by 3D imaging). Try finishing with a cold-water rinse as well.</p>
</div><div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">Can people with sensitive skin use it?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">In a 24-hour patch test (31 participants), it scored 0.00 for skin reaction and was rated non-irritating. If you have a skin condition, try it on a small area first, and consult a dermatologist if you notice any symptoms.</p>
</div><div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">Does it sting if it gets in my eyes?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">It may sting if it gets directly into your eyes, so rinse with water right away. In an eye irritation test (in vitro) using a cell model of the human cornea, it was classified as non-irritating.</p>
